# Documentation for /usr/local/bin/folk-around

folk-around is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) daemon for computer control.
It speaks MCP over stdio, HTTP SSE, or Cloudflare signaling plus local HTTP. The main runtime is Rust after migration; Zig remains the legacy daemon module and macOS menu bar app.

## Usage

    folk-around [options]

Options:
  --verbose      Show tool calls
  --mode <mode>  Security mode: full, limited, sandbox
  --stdio        Force stdio transport and ignore saved transport
  --http <port>  HTTP SSE transport mode (e.g. 8080)
  --p2p          Print pairing code, join saved/default signaling server, and start local HTTP
  --signal-server <url>  Custom signaling server URL
  --room <name>  Pairing code / signaling room name
  --help         This help

## Modes

full — unrestricted shell, full access
limited — safe-shell command allowlist
sandbox — current compatibility behavior uses the same safe-shell command allowlist; folk_spawn remains full-only

## Tools

folk_shell, folk_system_info, folk_list_apps, folk_spawn,
folk_clipboard_read, folk_clipboard_write, folk_screen_capture,
folk_ui_snapshot, folk_click, folk_type, folk_hotkey, folk_scroll,
folk_window, folk_app, folk_menu

## Transports

No transport flags: Reuse the saved HTTP port, or stdio if none is saved.
stdio: Use --stdio for MCP protocol over stdin/stdout. Pipe to any MCP client.
HTTP SSE: Use --http <port>. GET /sse for events, POST /message for calls.
Signaling: Use --p2p or --signal-server <url>. Prints a pairing code, joins /signal/<room>, starts local HTTP MCP, completes offer/answer, derives relay session keys from an X25519 shared secret, and encrypts relayed MCP payloads. The last server, code, port, and mode are saved under ~/.config/folk-around/config.

## Examples

  folk-around                                          # reuse saved HTTP port, or stdio if none is saved
  folk-around --stdio                                  # force stdio mode, full access
  folk-around --mode sandbox                          # safe-shell compatibility mode
  folk-around --http 8080                             # HTTP SSE on port 8080
  folk-around --signal-server folkaround.undivisible.dev
  echo '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}' | folk-around
